WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:16.400
Hello, John. It's Tuesday, January 9th. I'm
in Detroit, Michigan. It's very windy and

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.111
cold. I'm standing in the only place in the
continental United States where you can look

00:00:20.111 --> 00:00:27.980
south and see Canada, which you are doing
right now. I'm also standing in front of General

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:33.550
Motors headquarters. It's a very, very big
building.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:39.969
It's really nice of you to say that I live
in a way that is commensurate with my values.

00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:49.510
I haven't been feeling that way lately. For
the new year I drove to Spokane and I flew

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:55.639
to Reno and then I drove to Lake Tahoe. And
then I did that all in reverse for, like,

00:00:55.639 --> 00:01:03.229
a three day long party. And now, like a week
later, I've excepted an invitation from General

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:07.350
Motors to visit the North American International
Auto Show in Detroit, Michigan.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:12.549
I was invited to this because I write for
a few environmental blogs and there are some

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:18.640
environmental things going on here. Those
are my values. This is not my values.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.229
It's kind of difficult to convey what's really
going on here. It's a pretty gigantic spectacle.

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:32.270
I looked earlier, there's fake lichen on those
fake rocks. And up here, fake fire. I don't

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:41.530
even know how they're doing that; it's amazing.
And here we have the weirdest, prettiest fake

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.360
waterfall ever and it spells things.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:55.840
Right here, we have a Jeep that has got stuck
to a wall, and all the people in that Jeep

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:03.189
have had to jump out of the Jeep because they
were stuck to a wall.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:11.120
General Motors is giving away hot dogs to
a long line of people.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.980
So lame. Oh my god.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:27.530
[Girls]: Hi John! Hey John! See what you're
missing?

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.280
[Hank]: Ehhehehehehehehehehe, yeah.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.659
As for the Brotherhood 2.0 book club, I'm
really excited that you're giving me opportunities

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:38.959
to read so many books about genocide. I love
genocide. In terms of what you're going to

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:43.050
read, apparently none of our viewers want
you to read anything because they all want

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.209
you to write. So you should just go ahead
and read whatever it is you're writing. I'm

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:52.420
gonna make that your one option. You have
to read the book you are writing.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:57.760
And as for what to call it, you're gonna have
to give me some time. Also, it'd be nice to

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.579
know what it was about. I'd also like to say
happy birthday to Jessalyn Shields, a Brotherhood

00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:03.579
2.0 viewer and one of my best friends.

